reviews.body:
Independent lane52 review: **FIX `cc4dc5d2dcb1354e4a223fc02946ae7c42f1c961`**. Refs #19.

Reviewed an isolated `git archive` against exact base `bc8eeabfe5220e66a83be972b480a1d1ae8d87d2`; all 53 archived tracked blobs still match candidate tree `373b1a900ba251ee83ecb63a621371009810bc3c`. The delta is six additions within the three assigned phone-observations paths. The merged #9 recorder is unchanged.

Four reproducible P2 findings remain in `src/phone-observations/adapter.mjs`:

1. **F1 — recheck the GPS request token after sink delivery** ([lines 267–270](https://github.com/Bimbi-Dev/andes-hackathon/blob/cc4dc5d2dcb1354e4a223fc02946ae7c42f1c961/src/phone-observations/adapter.mjs#L267)). A synchronous local sink calls `stopLocation()` on `acquisition-request`. The session remains live, so acquisition continues despite the invalidated token: `getCurrentPosition` runs once and a new request timer is installed. Later `stop()` leaves that orphan timer behind. Actual: `{nativeCalls:1,timersAfterStop:1}`; expected both zero. This can initiate a potentially prompting sensor request after explicit stream cancellation. Match motion's token check before any further work; also ensure request-local timer ownership is retired on every cancellation path.

2. **F2 — validate elapsed deadlines when motion permission resolves** ([lines 353–372](https://github.com/Bimbi-Dev/andes-hackathon/blob/cc4dc5d2dcb1354e4a223fc02946ae7c42f1c961/src/phone-observations/adapter.mjs#L353)). Start a motion request, advance the injected wall and monotonic clocks by `maxSessionMs + 1`, defer timer execution, then resolve permission as granted. Actual: `{ok:true,listeners:1}` and the session remains started; expected rejection and zero motion listeners. The continuation checks identity/liveness but not elapsed request/session deadlines or current visibility before subscription. A bounded module must not depend solely on prompt/session timers executing on time; the adapter already handles delayed session timers at acquisition/callback entry. Revalidate before applying a grant or attaching the motion listener.

3. **F3 — an older passive query can overwrite a newer explicit denial** ([lines 146–160](https://github.com/Bimbi-Dev/andes-hackathon/blob/cc4dc5d2dcb1354e4a223fc02946ae7c42f1c961/src/phone-observations/adapter.mjs#L146), [129–135](https://github.com/Bimbi-Dev/andes-hackathon/blob/cc4dc5d2dcb1354e4a223fc02946ae7c42f1c961/src/phone-observations/adapter.mjs#L129)). Leave the initial permission query pending, deliver the location request's code-1 denial, then resolve that query with a conflicting granted status. Actual permission changes `denied → granted`, and another acquisition succeeds in the same session. The documented contract requires a new session after denied/revoked permission. A delayed conflicting monitor answer does not establish that the newer denial was resolved. Preserve the terminal/uncertain state or track observation/request ordering rather than letting the old answer reopen acquisition. This is a controlled conflicting-answer probe, not a claim that every browser returns that sequence.

4. **F4 — failed location callbacks lose acquisition options** ([lines 301–306](https://github.com/Bimbi-Dev/andes-hackathon/blob/cc4dc5d2dcb1354e4a223fc02946ae7c42f1c961/src/phone-observations/adapter.mjs#L301)). With `bufferCapacity:1`, `maximumAgeMs:12345`, `requestTimeoutMs:23456`, request a watch and deliver code 2. The retained error is only `{requestId:'1:geo:1',code:2}`; the request event is evicted and the local sink receives no error-bound acquisition settings. Expected the original `{enableHighAccuracy:false,maximumAge:12345,timeout:23456}` or a bounded recoverable request reference carrying them. A snapshot budget can help an export consumer, but an isolated error event cannot recover those values from the event's revision alone. This contradicts the documented per-request event provenance and the lane brief; preserve settings on failure as on success. Robert's merged [#9 review](https://github.com/Bimbi-Dev/andes-hackathon/pull/45#pullrequestreview-5560257204) likewise checks per-callback attribution through mutation/eviction; no backend reconciliation or unbounded request history is requested.

Verification on **Node 22.22.3**:

- `node --test tests/phone-observations/adapter.test.mjs tests/phone-capability/recorder.test.mjs`: **60 passed, 0 failed**, exit 0 (29 adapter + 31 recorder).
- Reviewer-owned 22-check suite derived from the preregistered P01–P18 checklist: **18 passed, 4 failed**, exit 1. Positive qualified synthetic GPS/motion paths, default qualification denial, default coordinate redaction, explicit precise consent/withdrawal, source/receipt separation, stale/reordered fixes, normal stop/restart, callback/event/request limits, unknown provenance and confounder non-classification all pass their baseline probes. Additional F1–F4 probes expose the gaps above; passing the baseline does not pass the affected checklist groups.
- A separate four-case minimal reproduction below also reports the four expected/actual mismatches, exit 1. Source files were never changed. Diff whitespace checks pass. The reviewer worktree remains clean at its original HEAD.

Live context read: PR52 had no reviews/issue comments/inline comments when captured; #19/#18 issue comment lists were empty. Read Robertzu43's merged PR45 reviews, including his exact-head positive attribution probe at `a6863e7c9f74b5c50b8e1674d47c97712dadacca`. Those recorder approvals are not approvals of this candidate.

Physical evidence remains **not-run/inconclusive**: all 106 #9 matrix rows, matched battery/data cost, device qualification and physical confounders remain unmeasured. Synthetic results are logic evidence only. Real streams remain disabled by default. Robert owns #18/#21; the provisional local boundary is appropriate and production transport/authentication/UI are outside this review. This verdict does not close #19, approve integration or authorize a pilot.

To reproduce, extract the exact candidate into a disposable directory and run the following with Node 22.22.3 from that directory. The fake platform never accesses device hardware, schedules real timers, installs anything or sends traffic. Each output has `passed`, `actual` and `expected`; the program exits 1 for the four demonstrated failures.


```sh
node --input-type=module <<'JS'
// Run from an immutable cc4dc5d2 archive; synthetic platform only, no device APIs.
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';
const root = process.env.ANDES_CANDIDATE_DIR ?? process.cwd();
const { createPhoneObservationAdapter: create, PROVISIONAL_BUDGET: B, QUALIFICATION_SCHEMA: Q } =
  await import(pathToFileURL(`${root}/src/phone-observations/adapter.mjs`));
const deferred = () => { let resolve; const promise = new Promise(r => { resolve = r; }); return { promise, resolve }; };
function fixture({ sink, budget = {} } = {}) {
  let mono = 100, next = 0, listenerCount = 0;
  const calls = [], events = [], timers = new Set(), query = deferred(), motion = deferred();
  const p = {
    isSecureContext: true, document: { visibilityState: 'visible', addEventListener() {}, removeEventListener() {} },
    navigator: { userActivation: { isActive: true }, permissions: { query: () => query.promise }, geolocation: {
      getCurrentPosition(ok, fail, opts) { calls.push({ ok, fail, opts }); },
      watchPosition(ok, fail, opts) { calls.push({ ok, fail, opts }); return 42; }, clearWatch() {},
    } },
    DeviceMotionEvent: { requestPermission: () => motion.promise },
    addEventListener(name) { if (name === 'devicemotion') listenerCount++; },
    removeEventListener(name) { if (name === 'devicemotion') listenerCount--; },
    setTimeout() { const id = ++next; timers.add(id); return id; }, clearTimeout(id) { timers.delete(id); },
  };
  const f = { calls, events, timers, query, motion, advance(ms) { mono += ms; }, listeners: () => listenerCount };
  f.a = create({ platform: p, clock: { now: () => ({ wallMs: 1800000000000 + mono, monoMs: mono }) },
    sink(event) { events.push(event); sink?.(event, f); }, mode: 'synthetic-test', contextKey: 'synthetic',
    qualification: { schema: Q, kind: 'synthetic-fixture', disposition: 'qualified', evidenceRef: 'review-only',
      contextKey: 'synthetic', budgetRevision: B.revision, streams: { geolocation: true, motion: true } },
    budget: { ...B, ...budget } });
  f.a.start({ sessionId: 'synthetic-session', tripId: 'synthetic-trip', revision: 'cc4dc5d2' });
  return f;
}
const results = [];
function check(id, actual, expected) {
  let passed = true;
  try { assert.deepEqual(actual, expected); } catch { passed = false; }
  results.push({ id, passed, actual, expected });
}
const f1 = fixture({ sink(e, f) { if (e.type === 'acquisition-request') f.a.stopLocation(); } });
f1.a.acquireLocation(); f1.a.stop();
check('F1', { nativeCalls: f1.calls.length, timersAfterStop: f1.timers.size }, { nativeCalls: 0, timersAfterStop: 0 });
const f2 = fixture(); const pending = f2.a.acquireMotion();
f2.advance(B.maxSessionMs + 1); f2.motion.resolve('granted'); const answer = await pending;
check('F2', { ok: answer.ok, listeners: f2.listeners() }, { ok: false, listeners: 0 }); f2.a.stop();
const f3 = fixture(); f3.a.acquireLocation(); f3.calls[0].fail({ code: 1 });
f3.query.resolve({ state: 'granted' }); await new Promise(r => setImmediate(r));
check('F3', { permission: f3.a.snapshot().permission.geolocation.state, retry: f3.a.acquireLocation().ok },
  { permission: 'denied', retry: false }); f3.a.stop();
const f4 = fixture({ budget: { bufferCapacity: 1, maximumAgeMs: 12345, requestTimeoutMs: 23456 } });
f4.a.acquireLocation({ watch: true }); f4.calls[0].fail({ code: 2 });
check('F4', f4.a.snapshot().events[0].data.options ?? null,
  { enableHighAccuracy: false, maximumAge: 12345, timeout: 23456 }); f4.a.stop();
console.log(JSON.stringify(results, null, 2));
process.exitCode = results.some(r => !r.passed) ? 1 : 0;
JS
```
